To build tcpdump under Windows, you need:

- version 6 (or higher) of Microsoft Visual Studio or the Cygnus gnu 
C compiler.
- The November 2001 (or later) edition of Microsoft Platform 
Software Development Kit (SDK), that contains some necessary includes 
for IPv6 support. You can download it from http://www.microsoft.com/sdk
- the separate WinPcap source distribution, which includes libpcap for
Win32. The sibling libpcap sources alone are not a WinPcap SDK; see
..\libpcap\README.Win32 for the upstream WinPcap build instructions.

First, extract tcpdump and WinPcap in the same folder, and build WinPcap.

The following paths are relative to this tcpdump source directory.

The Visual Studio workspace is win32\prj\WinDump.dsw. Its project
specifies win32\prj\release\WinDump.exe or win32\prj\debug\WinDump.exe.

The Cygwin makefile is win32\prj\GNUmakefile; its link target writes
windump.exe in that directory.
